  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform ring is rotating about the vertical axis with angular velocity&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>ω&nbsp;</mi></mrow></math>initially. A point insect (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>) having the same mass as that of the ring starts walking from the lowest point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and finally reaches the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;(as shown in the figure). The final angular velocity of the ring is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0028180_Question.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 123px; height: 152px;\" />",
